### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "UrbanNighttimeLaneChangeScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:actor1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow taxi vehicle making sudden lane change" .

:actor2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Black SUV following closely behind yellow taxi" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "White dashed lane marking being crossed by yellow taxi" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition ;
    :description "Nighttime urban environment with street lighting" .

:risk1 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Yellow taxi intruding into adjacent lane without signaling" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Black SUV at risk of rear-ending yellow taxi due to sudden lane change" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Potential distraction for other drivers due to sudden lane change in low visibility" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .
```

